From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:58:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wsdd2: seed without overflow

wsdd2 seeds its random numbers by shifting halves of its UUID left by
16 as an int, which overflows for half of all UUIDs, and has time()
write a time_t into an unsigned long, which is too small for it on a
32-bit target with a 64-bit time_t. Built with -fsanitize=undefined
-fsanitize-trap=undefined, wsdd2 traps on almost every start.

Add a patch that shifts as unsigned long and assigns time()'s result;
the seed srand48() takes stays the same.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 net/wsdd2/Makefile                            |  2 +-
 .../020-wsd-seed-without-overflow.patch       | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 net/wsdd2/patches/020-wsd-seed-without-overflow.patch

diff --git a/net/wsdd2/Makefile b/net/wsdd2/Makefile
index 7fde40c..edcbc80 100644
--- a/net/wsdd2/Makefile
+++ b/net/wsdd2/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=wsdd2
-PKG_RELEASE:=2
+PKG_RELEASE:=3
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://github.com/Netgear/wsdd2.git
diff --git a/net/wsdd2/patches/020-wsd-seed-without-overflow.patch b/net/wsdd2/patches/020-wsd-seed-without-overflow.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8c80c19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/net/wsdd2/patches/020-wsd-seed-without-overflow.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] wsd: seed without overflow
+
+set_seed() shifted the first 16 bits of each pair of the endpoint's
+UUID left by 16 as an int: for a value of 0x8000 or more, as half of
+all UUIDs have, the result does not fit, which is undefined behaviour.
+Built with -fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined, wsdd2 traps
+on almost every start. It also had time() write a time_t into an
+unsigned long, which is too small for it on a 32-bit target with a
+64-bit time_t.
+
+Shift as unsigned long, and assign time()'s result. srand48() takes the
+low 32 bits of its seed, which stay the same.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/wsd.c
++++ b/wsd.c
+@@ -95,10 +95,10 @@
+ 	uuid_endpoint(uuid);
+ 	uuid_parse(uuid, UUID);
+ 
+-	time((time_t *)&seed);
++	seed = time(NULL);
+ 	
+ 	for(size_t i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
+-		unsigned long s = UUID[2*i+1] | UUID[2*i+0] << 16;
++		unsigned long s = UUID[2*i+1] | (unsigned long)UUID[2*i+0] << 16;
+ 		seed ^= s;
+ 	}
+ 
